Begin3
Title:          Yasm
Version:        1.3.0
Entered-Date:   2019-11-22
Description:    Yasm is a complete rewrite of the NASM assembler. (UPX
                Compressed)
Summary:        Yasm is a complete rewrite of the NASM assembler under the
                "new" BSD License (some portions are under other licenses, see
                COPYING for details). Yasm currently supports the x86 and AMD64
                instruction sets, accepts NASM and GAS assembler syntaxes,
                outputs binary, ELF32, ELF64, 32 and 64-bit Mach-O, RDOFF2,
                COFF, Win32, and Win64 object formats, and generates source
                debugging information in STABS, DWARF 2, and CodeView 8
                formats. Yasm can be easily integrated into Visual Studio
                2005/2008 and 2010 for assembly of NASM or GAS syntax code into
                Win32 or Win64 object files.
Keywords:       nasm, asm, gas, yasm, assembler, assembly, DJGPP, Visual Studio
Author:         Peter Johnson and others
Maintained-By:  Peter Johnson
Defunct-Original-Site:   http://yasm.tortall.net
Primary-Site: http://github.com/yasm/yasm
Platforms:      DOS
Copying-Policy: Simplified (2-Clause) BSD License and Revised (3-Clause) BSD License
End
